     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m using a small test sample with only 10k paired-end reads in them. However, the reference sequences and the annotation files are 7.5 GB and 571MB, respectively. The data are not yet published so I&#39;d rather not share them via link here in the discussion grop. Contact me if you want to access them. I can share some basic information about the reference sequences in the meantime, maybe this can provide some insight as to why it is so slow:</div><div><br></div><div><ul><li>Each reference sequence is annotated with a single gene_id, across its entire length. <br></li><li>The sequence lengths are varying between 109-45500 bases, with a mean of 485 and a median of 643.</li><li>The sequence header lengths vary between 30-57 characters in length, with a mean of 45 and a median of 43. </li></ul><div>Thanks for your time looking into this.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Fredrik</div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div></div>"
